# DIAGNOSTICS

When a program can't be linked, `Process.start` throws, and the starter prints `process start:` and why, naming the object: a library bootfs's `lib/` doesn't have, an undefined symbol, a relocation type that isn't supported, or general-dynamic TLS.

# BUGS

Libraries come only from the bootfs image the program came from.
Nothing checks that a program and its libraries come from the same build.
